Brook, you're right that in the case of running multiple chains, the $samples object returned by nimble is a list, where each element of the list contains a matrix of samples from a single MCMCchain ($samples$chain1, etc...).  Is a matrix of posterior samples a format which the posterior package will recognize?

If so, then you can provide the samples from each individual chain using samples$chain1, samples$chain2, etc, or you can also easily combine the posterior samples from all chains into a single matrix, using:

matrix_of_all_samples <- do.call(rbind, samples)

Then use that matrix_of_all_samples object with the posterior package.

I hope this helps,
Daniel

