Hi all,

I am hoping someone can offer a hint on writing what should be a simple function. From the nimble virtual workshop of 2021 <https://htmlpreview.github.io/?https://github.com/nimble-training/nimble-virtual-2021/blob/master/overview.html>, at the end of section 5, there is an exercise to write a function for a vectorized dnorm. Below is some sample code for what I have so far, where if I set returnType(double(1)) I get an error from nimbleModel() about returnType, but if I use returnType(double(0)) it returns only the first entry of the vector (obviously). I am using nimble 0.12.1 and I should mention that I did not attend the workshop, so that may be part of the problem! Any suggestions would be greatly appreciated.

Best,
Adrian

library(nimble)

code <- nimbleCode({
  intercept ~ dnorm(0, sd = 1000)
  slope ~ dnorm(0, sd = 1000)
  sigma ~ dunif(0, 100)
  predicted.y[1:4]  <- intercept + slope * x[1:4] # vectorized node
  y[1:4] ~ dnorm_vec(predicted.y[1:4], sd = sigma)
})

my_dnorm <- nimbleFunction( run = function(x = double(1), mean = double(1), sd = double(0), log = logical(0, default = 0)) { returnType(double(1)) logdens <- dnorm(x, mean, sd, log = TRUE) if(log) return(logdens) else return(exp(logdens)) })

## Test (this works)
c_dnorm_vec <- compileNimble(dnorm_vec)
c_dnorm_vec(1:10, mean = rep(2, 10), sd = 0.5, log = TRUE)

# This returns an error about returnType
model <- nimbleModel(code, inits = list(slope = rnorm(1), sigma = runif(1),
intercept = rnorm(1)), data = list(y = runif(4), x = runif(4)*10))

