hi Adrian,

y[1:4] in this case is considered by nimble as a multivariate node, which should have a scalar-valued logProb.
So you need to have your dmnorm_vec return a scalar that is the sum of the log density values for the elements, and of course change the returnType to double(0) (or equivalently double()).

Side note: the code you provided named your nimbleFunction my_dnorm, when it should be dnorm_vec to be consistent with the rest of the code.

-chris

