Hi there. I am also getting the slice sampler warning that is the subject of this thread. However, unlike others, I don't think my initial values are invalid. My model seems to run with no errors in JAGS. The NIMBLE version of my model is attached. In short, I am running a community multi-scale occupancy model informed by nested data (detections at fine-scale survey points nested within 1-km^2 grid cells, with max 16 points per grid cell), wherein fine-scale point occupancy is informed summaries of the number of points occupied by each species within each grid cell. Moreover, I have a time-removal component wherein detection probability is informed by the timing of detections within a 6-min survey.

In most cases, the full array of 16 points is surveyed per grid cell each year, but in some cases, only a subset of the 16 possible points are surveyed. My point level process model is:

z[j, i] ~ dbin(psi[j, i] * Z[j, i], n.point[j]),

wherein 'z' is the latent point level occupancy state for species i during grid cell X year j, 'psi' is the probability of a point being occupied conditional on the grid cell being occupied, and 'n.point' is the number of points surveyed during grid cell X year occasion j. I've set the initial values for 'z' to the number of points surveyed, 'n.point'.

The repeated warnings I get are:

Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[220, 4]'. Current parameter value is 4.
Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[220, 15]'. Current parameter value is 4.
Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[655, 48]'. Current parameter value is 16.
Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[131, 63]'. Current parameter value is 8.
Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[358, 63]'. Current parameter value is 13.
Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[655, 65]'. Current parameter value is 16.
Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[579, 78]'. Current parameter value is 16.
Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[303, 90]'. Current parameter value is 4.
Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[383, 92]'. Current parameter value is 4.
Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[540, 95]'. Current parameter value is 15.
Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[127, 106]'. Current parameter value is 8.
Warning: slice sampler reached maximum number of contractions for 'z[217, 139]'. Current parameter value is 5.

For all of the problem nodes listed, the slice sampler appears to be stuck at `n.point', i.e., the number of points surveyed for that occasion. For example, n.point[217] = 5 and n.point[540] = 15.  Would it be better to set it to the number of points where the species was actually detected? I checked several of these cases, and in all that I have looked at the species was not detected at any of the points within the corresponding grid cell (e.g., Y.sum[217, 139], Y.sum[127,106], and Y.sum[540,95] all equal zero.

