Hi,

I hope someone can help because I'm a bit stuck. We are modeling count data and trying to account for zero-inflation and overdispersion using a ZINB model. We are parameterizing the model in NIMBLE using a gamma-poisson mixture model for the negative binomial.  Basically, what appears to be happening is that the r parameter isn't initializing (see figure ).

We believe this is why our model is not converging, but we don't see anything obviously wrong with our model configuration (model code below). We would appreciate any input on what we can do to fix this. Also, we have already fit this model as a ZIP and had no issues with convergence, so it appears that adding the rho parameter to transform it to a ZINB is the cause of the issues.

Thanks in advance!
Chandra

Below is our Nimble code:

#Priors
      a.psi ~ dnorm(0, 0.01)
      tau <- 1/sig^2
      sig ~ dgamma(2, 0.5)
      b1.p ~ dnorm(0, 0.01)
      b2.p ~ dnorm(0, 0.01)
      b3.p ~ dnorm(0, 0.01)
      b0.p ~ dnorm(0, 0.01)
      r ~ dgamma(0.01, 0.01)

 #beta cov priors
      for(n in 1:nenvcov){
        b.pois[n] ~ dnorm(0, 0.1)
      }

      #CAR priors
      for(n in 1:2){
        u[1:ncgrid, n] ~ dcar_proper(muu[1:ncgrid, n], C[1:L], adj[1:L], num[1:ncgrid], M[1:ncgrid], tauu[n], gammau[n])
        tauu[n] <- 1/sdu[n]^2
        sdu[n] ~ dgamma(2, 0.5)
        gammau[n] ~ dunif(bou[1], bou[2])

        mu0[n] ~ dnorm(0, 0.1) #use this if we don't want the CAR to be zero-centered

        for(m in 1:ncgrid){
          muu[m, n] <- mu0[n]
          #muu[m, n] <- 0
        }#n

      }#m

      u1 <- mean(u[1:ncgrid, 1])
      u2 <- mean(u[1:ncgrid, 2])

#Count/Abundance model - ZINB
      for(k in 1:ngrid){
        for(j in 1:nsurv){
          y[k, j] ~ dpois(lambda.star[k, j])
          lambda.star[k, j] <- lambda[k, j] * z[k, j] * rho[k, j]
          log(lambda[k, j]) <- log(theta[k, j]) + e[k, j]
          z[k, j] ~ dbern(psi[k, j])
          log(theta[k, j]) <- u[gridID[k], 1] + inprod(envcov[k, j, 1:nenvcov], b.pois[1:nenvcov])
          logit(psi[k, j]) <- a.psi + b1.p*sea1[j, surveyID[k]] + b2.p*sea2[j, surveyID[k]] + b3.p*sea3[j, surveyID[k]]
          rho[k, j] ~ dgamma(r, r)
     }#j
      }#k

#Some initial values
  inits <- list(u = structure(.Data= runif(const$ncgrid * 2, -.1, .1),.Dim=c(const$ncgrid, 2)),
                sdu = runif(2, 2, 4),
                mu0 = c(runif(1, -1, 0), runif(1, 3, 5)),
                a.psi = runif(1, -1, 1),
                b.pois = runif(const$nenvcov),
                b.size = runif(const$nenvcov))

